Nothing.

57
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:43,720
I don't think he's going to come back this time.

58
00:08:43,720 --> 00:08:45,720
What will you do?

59
00:08:45,720 --> 00:08:49,720
Nothing. It's better for him if he doesn't come back.

60
00:08:49,720 --> 00:08:51,720
But why?

61
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:55,720
Because of what happened after the last battle.

62
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:58,720
Why did you ignore my orders?

63
00:08:58,720 --> 00:09:00,720
I apologize.

64
00:09:00,720 --> 00:09:03,720
I'm the one who's in charge of your operations, aren't I?

65
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,720
Yes.

66
00:09:04,720 --> 00:09:08,720
You do know you're supposed to obey my orders, understand?

67
00:09:08,720 --> 00:09:09,720
Yes.

68
00:09:09,720 --> 00:09:11,720
I'm warning you not to do it again.

69
00:09:11,720 --> 00:09:12,720
Yes.

70
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,720
Hey, are you even listening to anything I'm saying?

71
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:15,720
Yes.

72
00:09:15,720 --> 00:09:16,720
Oh, no, you don't.

73
00:09:16,720 --> 00:09:20,720
You're not going to get out of this by just saying yes to everything I say.

74
00:09:20,720 --> 00:09:22,720
I know, Miss Misato.

75
00:09:22,720 --> 00:09:25,720
We won, didn't we? Isn't that enough?

76
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:29,720
You know, it may seem easy going along with whatever anyone else wants,

77
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:32,720
but if you get into an Eva with that attitude, it'll kill you.

78
00:09:32,720 --> 00:09:35,720
You know, I just don't care anymore.

79
00:09:35,720 --> 00:09:38,720
It'd be nice if I could say you've got the right attitude,

80
00:09:38,720 --> 00:09:42,720
but if you think you're going to get any praise out of me, you're wrong, Shinji.

81
00:09:42,720 --> 00:09:43,720
That's not the point.

82
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,720
Anyway, I'm the only one who can pilot it.

83
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:48,720
I'll just have to do.

84
00:09:48,720 --> 00:09:49,720
I see.

85
00:09:49,720 --> 00:10:00,720
If getting into the Eva means nothing but pain to him, I don't think he should pilot again.

86
00:10:00,720 --> 00:10:02,720
Otherwise, he'll be killed.

87
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,720
But we need pilots.

88
00:10:12,720 --> 00:10:13,720
Captain!

89
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,720
Ida, go on ahead.

90
00:10:16,720 --> 00:10:19,720
But I can't go on and leave you behind like this.

91
00:10:19,720 --> 00:10:20,720
What will I do?

92
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,720
You fool!

93
00:10:32,720 --> 00:10:34,720
There.

94
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,720
The new kid!

95
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:45,720
Ikari!

96
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:04,560
Told you was real sorry about everything.

97
00:11:05,140 --> 00:11:07,440
His kid's sister really tore him a new one.

98
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:10,860
She said that it was the robot who saved her lives.

99
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:13,220
That must be pretty embarrassing,

100
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,700
getting herself chewed out by a second grader.

101
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:16,920
Right?

102
00:11:20,880 --> 00:11:21,360
Hmm.

103
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:23,160
I like it out here at night

104
00:11:23,160 --> 00:11:25,360
because those noisy cicadas don't chirp.

105
00:11:25,880 --> 00:11:27,800
It was pretty quiet when I was a kid,

106
00:11:27,960 --> 00:11:29,320
but there are tons of them now.

107
00:11:31,180 --> 00:11:32,040
Misato said...

108
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:32,180
Huh?

109
00:11:32,720 --> 00:11:35,640
That the ego system is returning to its former state.

110
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,400
Misato said so, hmm?

111
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:38,820
I really envy you.

112
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,000
I mean, you live with such a beautiful woman

113
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:43,120
and you get the power of the Evangelion.

114
00:11:43,240 --> 00:11:43,880
Oh, man.

115
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:48,040
I wish I could get inside that lovely cockpit just once.

116
00:11:48,900 --> 00:11:50,580
You really shouldn't, you know.

117
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,760
Your mother would probably be worried.

118
00:11:53,540 --> 00:11:53,780
Huh?

119
00:11:54,560 --> 00:11:56,320
Oh, don't worry about my mother.

120
00:11:56,320 --> 00:11:58,220
I don't have one of those.

121
00:11:58,740 --> 00:11:59,040
Oh.

122
00:11:59,940 --> 00:12:01,520
I'm no different from you.

123
00:12:01,520 --> 00:12:06,460
You'll take something to eat, won't you?

124
00:12:07,180 --> 00:12:07,700
Yeah.

125
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:11,360
Do you usually do things like this?

126
00:12:12,040 --> 00:12:12,920
Well, sure.

127
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,920
Is it some kind of training for guerrilla warfare or something?

128
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,560
How could I fight with toys like these?

129
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,880
It's just for fun.

130
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:34,600
You're Shinji Akari, aren't you?

131
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:35,220
Huh?

132
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:35,320
Hmm?

133
00:12:38,280 --> 00:12:38,880
Hey!

134
00:12:39,820 --> 00:12:40,120
Ah!

135
00:12:46,400 --> 00:12:48,660
You're Shinji Akari, aren't you?

136
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:49,620
Yes.

137
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,420
We're from the Nerve Security Intelligence.

138
00:12:53,500 --> 00:12:55,360
Under Security Clause Article 8,

139
00:12:55,640 --> 00:12:57,380
we're taking you to Nerve Headquarters.

140
00:12:57,800 --> 00:12:58,180
All right?

141
00:12:58,180 --> 00:12:59,420
Yes.

142
00:13:04,300 --> 00:13:06,060
And all you did was stand there?

143
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,820
That's easy for you to say,

144
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:11,420
but they were nerve intelligence professionals.

145
00:13:11,980 --> 00:13:13,440
So what about it?

146
00:13:13,740 --> 00:13:16,140
Jeez, don't you have any balls at all?

147
00:13:16,940 --> 00:13:18,740
Girl, pervert, ape.

148
00:13:18,820 --> 00:13:21,060
Only an idiot fights when he knows you can't win.

149
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:23,060
Balls have nothing to do with it.

150
00:13:23,060 --> 00:13:36,740
Long time no see.

151
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:37,680
Yeah.

152
00:13:38,480 --> 00:13:41,840
Do you feel any better after wandering around for two days?

153
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,240
I don't know.

154
00:13:44,140 --> 00:13:45,420
The Ava is on standby.

155
00:13:45,600 --> 00:13:46,520
Will you pilot it?

156
00:13:47,280 --> 00:13:48,280
Or won't you?

157
00:13:49,800 --> 00:13:52,040
You're not going to scold me for running away?

158
00:13:52,040 --> 00:13:57,220
Of course you're not.

159
00:13:57,540 --> 00:13:59,220
I'm no relation to you, am I?

160
00:14:00,780 --> 00:14:03,240
If I say that I won't pilot Unit 1,

161
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:04,940
what are you going to do with it?

162
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,360
I suppose that Rey will do it.

163
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:09,540
You won't pilot it?

164
00:14:10,340 --> 00:14:12,840
It seems a little bit unrealistic

165
00:14:12,840 --> 00:14:15,080
for you to force everything on her.

166
00:14:15,860 --> 00:14:16,620
Don't worry.

167
00:14:16,980 --> 00:14:17,780
I'll pilot it.

168
00:14:18,260 --> 00:14:20,160
But you don't want to do it.

169
00:14:20,280 --> 00:14:21,120
Of course not.

170
00:14:21,120 --> 00:14:23,960
It's not something that comes to me naturally.

171
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:26,620
But Ayanami and you and Miss Ritsuko...

172
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:28,580
Stop that line of crap!

173
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,220
This has nothing to do with any of us.

174
00:14:31,560 --> 00:14:33,040
If you don't like it, get out of here.

175
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,020
Just forget all about Ava and us

176
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:36,500
and go back where you came from.

177
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:39,780
We don't need someone with that attitude, piloting.

178
00:14:39,780 --> 00:14:57,340
You do know that the third child is leaving Tokyo 3 tomorrow, don't you?

179
00:14:57,340 --> 00:15:00,100
We'll reconfigure Unit 1's system for Rey.

180
00:15:01,560 --> 00:15:04,880
Regardless of the results of the Unit 0 reactivation experiments,

181
00:15:05,180 --> 00:15:07,320
we'll move on to experimenting on Unit 1.

182
00:15:12,080 --> 00:15:14,560
According to the Marduk organization's report,

183
00:15:14,940 --> 00:15:17,140
the fourth child hasn't been found yet.

184
00:15:17,140 --> 00:15:20,900
Does that mean we can't get any more pilot recruits?

185
00:15:20,900 --> 00:15:24,820
Uh, excuse me.

186
00:15:25,280 --> 00:15:26,740
Where is Miss Misato?

187
00:15:27,360 --> 00:15:28,920
I'd like to say goodbye.

188
00:15:29,260 --> 00:15:31,080
You are no longer NERV personnel.

189
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,680
Therefore, we can't give you that information.

190
00:15:33,680 --> 00:15:47,520
Hey, Kari!

191
00:15:47,880 --> 00:15:48,100
Huh?

192
00:15:48,100 --> 00:15:49,400
Hey, you left this stuff behind!

193
00:15:49,400 --> 00:15:49,580
Oh!

194
00:15:59,060 --> 00:16:00,540
Uh, excuse me.

195
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,100
Could I...

196
00:16:02,100 --> 00:16:02,600
Um...

197
00:16:02,600 --> 00:16:05,980
Well...

198
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:06,960
Thank you.

199
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,020
Hey, Tauji!

200
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:11,900
Come on, say something!

201
00:16:14,900 --> 00:16:15,760
Kari, look.

202
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,560
I'm sorry about hitting you twice.

203
00:16:17,800 --> 00:16:19,400
Please, you gotta hit me back.

204
00:16:19,740 --> 00:16:20,980
I can't do that!

205
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:21,720
You gotta.

206
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,500
Otherwise, I won't be satisfied.

207
00:16:23,800 --> 00:16:25,720
He's a pretty embarrassing guy, isn't he?

208
00:16:26,060 --> 00:16:27,760
But if it'll put an end to this dispute,

209
00:16:27,940 --> 00:16:29,260
why don't you go ahead and hit him?

210
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:31,280
But I...

211
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:31,920
Hurry up!

212
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,580
You don't have much time, do you?

213
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:34,620
Okay.

214
00:16:35,140 --> 00:16:36,060
But only once.

215
00:16:36,720 --> 00:16:37,140
Right!

216
00:16:37,480 --> 00:16:38,180
Come on!

217
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:43,220
Hey, wait!

218
00:16:43,220 --> 00:16:47,020
Don't hold back.

219
00:16:47,020 --> 00:16:52,320
Oh, that hurt.

220
00:16:52,320 --> 00:17:04,620
How do you know I'd be here?

221
00:17:04,620 --> 00:17:06,360
Uh, it was just a hunch.

222
00:17:06,360 --> 00:17:08,760
We've seen lots of other classmates off before.

223
00:17:08,980 --> 00:17:10,540
It's getting to be a regular thing.

224
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:14,960
Of course, if you're leaving, you know,

225
00:17:15,140 --> 00:17:18,160
we'll have to leave this city sometime soon.

226
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:20,240
But we can't really blame you for that.

227
00:17:20,620 --> 00:17:23,360
I mean, we saw how you suffered in the Eva.

228
00:17:23,360 --> 00:17:28,700
Uh, and anyway, if anyone does try to blame you,

229
00:17:29,040 --> 00:17:31,520
I'm gonna give him a whop on the head!

230
00:17:35,160 --> 00:17:36,100
Come on!

231
00:17:36,220 --> 00:17:37,420
Try not to look so gloomy.

232
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:39,060
Take care, Ikari.

233
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:40,540
Yeah, take care.

234
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:41,360
Well, uh...

235
00:17:41,360 --> 00:17:43,700
Your time is up.

236
00:17:43,700 --> 00:17:43,980
Huh?

237
00:17:43,980 --> 00:17:45,980
Uh...

238
00:17:45,980 --> 00:18:14,660
I'm the one who deserved to be hit, not you!

239
00:18:14,660 --> 00:18:16,340
I'm a coward!

240
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:18,660
I'm dishonest!

241
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:20,840
I'm sneaky!

242
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:22,840
And a wimp!

243
00:18:24,080 --> 00:18:25,900
Don't give us any more trouble.

244
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,060
Jeez!

245
00:18:37,620 --> 00:18:40,060
Well, he's gone.

246
00:18:40,060 --> 00:18:45,720
Do you really think this is for the best?

247
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,640
The hedgehog's dilemma.

248
00:18:48,980 --> 00:18:51,920
The closer we become, the more deeply we hurt.

249
00:18:53,100 --> 00:18:54,320
Now I understand.

250
00:18:54,320 --> 00:18:59,900
I finally understand.

251
00:19:00,320 --> 00:19:03,600
He can't let others know how he feels in any other way.

